    "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
    "description": "The lesson focuses on heuristics and cognitive biases in decision-making, exploring how these mental shortcuts influence choices in daily life and the professional environment. The aim is to understand that, while useful for simplifying decisions in uncertain contexts, heuristics can generate distortions, misperceptions, and systematic errors. At the same time, analyzing biases allows for the recognition of thought patterns that affect diverse areas such as business, health, and finance, offering insights to improve the quality of individual and organizational decisions.",
